  <article class="narrow page-intro prose"><p class="eyebrow">Terms</p><h1>Read the proposal in context.</h1><p class="lead">O2AT v0.2 is an engineering draft. It is provided for technical review and does not establish product support or certification.</p><h2>Technical status</h2><p>Specifications and interactive demonstrations are proposals or illustrations unless a page identifies independent measurement evidence. Do not treat the paper as a ratified standard, compatibility guarantee, safety certification, manufacturer endorsement, patent clearance or proof of audible performance.</p><h2>Third-party material</h2><p>External standards, vendor names, products and technical references remain the property of their respective owners. Their citation is for contextual review and is not an endorsement.</p><h2>Open work</h2><p>Software, RTL, hardware and specification licensing are separate matters. The draft’s proposed licensing direction does not silently assign rights to third-party material or certify an implementation.</p></article>
